orchadOS: the ROS 2 node reads each IMU packet once.

Upstream: unitreerobotics/unilidar_sdk2 pull request #33 (open), its change to
this file, unchanged. timer_callback() called getImuData() twice per IMU packet;
the first call consumed the packet, so the if() saw nothing and /unilidar/imu was
published rarely or never.

Made on upstream commit 0e3c51f512e6b8ff60b8c32f160b412cb48445c2 (v2.0.10);
services/kit-recorder/setup/install.sh pins it (UNILIDAR_COMMIT).

diff --git a/unitree_lidar_ros2/src/unitree_lidar_ros2/include/unitree_lidar_ros2.h b/unitree_lidar_ros2/src/unitree_lidar_ros2/include/unitree_lidar_ros2.h
index 29c094c..7e30d1c 100644
--- a/unitree_lidar_ros2/src/unitree_lidar_ros2/include/unitree_lidar_ros2.h
+++ b/unitree_lidar_ros2/src/unitree_lidar_ros2/include/unitree_lidar_ros2.h
@@ -165,8 +165,9 @@ void UnitreeLidarSDKNode::timer_callback()
     if (result == LIDAR_IMU_DATA_PACKET_TYPE)
     {
         LidarImuData imu;
-        lsdk_->getImuData(imu);
-
+        // Upstream bug: getImuData() was called twice, draining the queue
+        // before the publish path could see the message. Single-call form
+        // below uses the data from the same fetch the if() consumed.
         if (lsdk_->getImuData(imu))
         {
             // publish imu message
